  <!-- John's Vision -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="community-layout">
        <div class="community-text">
          <h2>John's vision</h2>
          <p>John Knights has spent over 15 years in wildlife rescue. Holding a permit from the Queensland Department of Environment, Tourism, Science and Innovation (DETSI) for koala rescue, he founded Koala Rescue Brisbane South Inc. with a simple belief that every koala in need deserves compassionate care, no matter the time, the weather or how hard it is to reach.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">What started as one person with a mission has grown into something remarkable. A growing team of dedicated local volunteers, each bringing unique skills and genuine passion, now responds to koalas in need across Brisbane south.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">John mentors every volunteer. He believes the best rescuers are made, not found. He's committed to building a team that will outlast any single individual.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="community-image">
          <img src="website-images/Koala climbing tree close-up.jpg" alt="Koala climbing a eucalyptus tree, looking towards the camera" loading="lazy" style="object-position: center 65%;">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How We Work -->
  <section class="section section--light">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="community-layout">
        <div class="community-image">
          <img src="website-images/Koala reaching up tree trunk.jpg" alt="Koala reaching up a tree trunk after being released back into its home range" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="community-text">
          <h2>How we work</h2>
          <p>When someone calls, we respond — 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. Trained volunteers arrive with the right equipment, the right knowledge and the right attitude to get the job done safely.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">But we don't just rescue. We assess, we relocate when necessary and we reunite animals with their habitat after a stay in the wildlife hospital. Every rescue is documented. Every case is a chance to help protect our koalas.</p>
          <ul class="about-how-list">
            <li>
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined">phone_in_talk</span>
              <div><strong>You phone.</strong> We answer. <strong>Please don't text or message.</strong> Phone calls allow us to ask the right questions and to respond promptly.</div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined">directions_car</span>
              <div><strong>We come to you.</strong> A trained volunteer heads out, whatever the hour, with the equipment needed for the situation.</div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined">healing</span>
              <div><strong>We assess and act.</strong> After assessment, this may involve safe capture, relocation, monitoring, transport to veterinary care or hopefully, no action because the koala is perfectly fine where it is.</div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined">park</span>
              <div><strong>We return them home.</strong> After a wildlife hospital visit, we release the koalas back into suitable habitat in their home range.</div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The People -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="community-layout">
        <div class="community-text">
          <h2>The people behind the mission</h2>
          <p>From the person who spots a koala in need on their morning walk to the rescuer who drives out at midnight, everyone plays a vital role. We celebrate each other, support each other and make decisions together.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">We're always looking for volunteer phone coordinators, first responders, rescuers, rescue support crews, trap sitters, transporters, admin organisers and of course, community advocates. They're not just titles; they're the roles of local people who care.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">We communicate regularly, ensuring that we stay sharp, connected and ready.</p>
          <div style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            <a href="volunteer.html" class="btn">Join the team</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="community-image">
          <img src="website-images/Koala Party Griffith Uni Nathan campus October 11 2025.jpg" alt="KRBS volunteer team at the Koala Party event at Griffith University Nathan campus" loading="lazy">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

